# Folders that hold other people's workspaces, not this one.
# mine.py skips these when mining Mimir itself, so the self-mine measures
# Mimir rather than Mimir plus six fixtures.
#
# checks/fixtures is test material: ten deliberately near-identical findings
# and a deliberately broken workspace. Measuring them alongside the doctrine
# reports the near-duplication as a canonical-source problem, which is a
# confident wrong reading of a folder that is doing exactly what it should.
eval
checks/fixtures
self-evidence.json
